  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-04T03:09:17.956Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As a side request to my other post to have higher bit rate audio streaming.\nAVPro is capable of doing up to 7.1 channel audio streaming however due to a limitation in the default Windows Media Foundation decoder inside of it, we are limited to 5.1. Having the extra channels of audio would be useful for doing a 5.1.2 setup for Dolby Atmos integration. or advanced custom immersive discrete layouts.\nWould it be possible to use a different decoder that allows for higher bitrate and more multichannel support?",
